                <pb facs="0147" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg43"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Mizner</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 31,
                        1890</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Wharton instructs Mr. Ryan, at the City of Mexico, to telegraph Mr. Mizner
                    that the Department directs him to proceed to San José de Guatemala immediately,
                    there to await further instructions, after providing for communication with the
                    naval vessels of the United States at that port and arranging prompt telegraphic
                    facilities with the legation at Guatemala City, and thence with Mr. Ryan, at the
                    City of Mexico. Also to answer this instruction through the legation in Mexico
                    promptly.</p>
            </div>
